commit c21a630dcd28b2473a7fa9ee964ded59a4df213d

C03: a YouTube search opens YouTube's results page under review, and researching what something is searches that something (WEB1481)

«buscá videos de gatos en youtube» reached no reader (no operation at all); `_youtube_search_query` now reads «busca X en youtube» / «busca en youtube X» as one reviewed browser.navigate to https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=… with the person's literal query — the YouTube twin of the WEB1455 installed-browser search — and never a playback («reproduce … en youtube» stays media.play.youtube). «Investiga en internet que es el h2o» searched the whole question, got nothing relevant and said «sobre el tema» (WEB1467); `_research_question_subject` now reads the who/what question inside a research order as its subject («h2o», article dropped, same exclusions as the who-is reader), the search uses that subject and the composer answers with what a snippet states, naming the page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


